479	/// Bytes of messages the PROCESS may hold in flight across every open
480	/// mailbox's worker pool and reorder buffer (see the module docs,
481	/// "Parallelism", and [`shared_budget`]). One message over this is admitted on
482	/// its own, so a 64 MB message (the `MAX_EML` cap) never deadlocks the
483	/// pipeline; it just runs alone.
